Make close_MBR() safe to call at any time, and free the old voice in init_MBR().

eSpeak NG drives MBROLA through the one-channel library API
(init_MBR/close_MBR/...). Two problems in that API:

1. close_MBR() dereferenced its globals unconditionally, so calling it
   before a voice had been loaded (or twice) crashed. eSpeak NG's POSIX
   path does exactly that when selecting an MBROLA voice.
2. init_MBR() overwrote the globals without releasing the previous voice,
   so every voice switch leaked the whole diphone database (several MB).
   This is the path eSpeak NG takes on Windows when the user changes
   voices in NVDA.

close_MBR() now checks and clears each global, and init_rename_MBR()
calls it first.

diff --git a/LibOneChannel/onechannel.c b/LibOneChannel/onechannel.c
index 97bb6a2..65c8687 100644
--- a/LibOneChannel/onechannel.c
+++ b/LibOneChannel/onechannel.c
@@ -110,6 +110,10 @@ int DLL_EXPORT init_rename_MBR(char *dbaname,char* rename_string,char* clone_str
 	freopen("mbrola.log","wt",stderr);
 #endif
 
+	/* Loading a new voice must release the previous one, otherwise every
+	 * voice switch leaks the whole diphone database. */
+	close_MBR();
+
 	if (rename_string)
     {
 		rename_list= init_ZStringList();
@@ -162,13 +166,15 @@ int DLL_EXPORT init_MBR(char *dbaname)
 }
 
 void DLL_EXPORT close_MBR(void)
-/*	Free all the allocated memory */
+/*	Free all the allocated memory
+ *	Safe to call when nothing is initialized, and more than once.
+ */
 {
-	close_Mbrola(my_brole);
-	my_parse->close_Parser(my_parse);   /* ... the parser   */
-	close_InputFifo(my_input);
-	close_Fifo(my_fifo);
-	my_dba->close_Database(my_dba); /* ... the database */
+	if (my_brole) { close_Mbrola(my_brole); my_brole= NULL; }
+	if (my_parse) { my_parse->close_Parser(my_parse); my_parse= NULL; }  /* ... the parser   */
+	if (my_input) { close_InputFifo(my_input); my_input= NULL; }
+	if (my_fifo)  { close_Fifo(my_fifo); my_fifo= NULL; }
+	if (my_dba)   { my_dba->close_Database(my_dba); my_dba= NULL; }   /* ... the database */
 }
 
 int DLL_EXPORT reset_MBR() 
